   "evidence": "The window depends only on the confirmed row and the in-memory anchor: `function open(h) { const a = anchors.get(key(h.repo, h.ref)); if (!current(h) || a?.tip !== store.leaseRow(...)?.confirmed?.tip) return false; return windowOpen(a?.anchor ?? null, clock.sample()); }` (82-86). When a release ends `unconfirmed` the code just does `return wait` (186) and when it ends `unchanged` it drops the intent and returns wait (195-199). Neither path closes the window. The row stays confirmed `held` at generation 1 and the anchor is unchanged, so `windowOpen(h1)` stays true even though the released tip lets another member acquire. The unconfirmed case (lost response) is ordinary. The unchanged-then-applied-later case is rarer."
