  "title": "Reconcile a pending never-confirmed acquisition before deciding another run's acquisition",
  "file": "src/integrations/leases.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "One run fails to acquire an absent claim and leaves an unresolved attempt behind. When another run tries after the service becomes readable again, it is refused without checking that ownership remains available.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test \"$TMPDIR/lease-adjudication/regressions.test.ts\"",
    "output": "Using HEAD's fixture with the supplied cross-run regression:\nF3 {\"result\":{\"kind\":\"refused\",\"reason\":\"live\"},\"refReads\":0,\"pending\":true}\nAssertion failed: Expected \"held\", Received \"refused\"."
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD returns before reconciliation: `if (row && row.runId !== want.run && (row.intent || row.confirmed?.state === \"held\")) return refused;`, followed by `const settled = await reconcile(repo, ref, signal);`. Thus a never-confirmed acquisition belonging to another run cannot reach reconciliation through this operation. At base, reconcileLeaseIntent already drops an acquisition intent when the ref remains absent; the new manager's ordering prevents that mechanism from running. The later commit reconciles first, returns wait for unresolved intents, then checks remaining confirmed ownership."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Run A's first claim attempt hits a network blip and is left pending, although GitHub never applied it. When run B later tries to claim the same, still-unclaimed ref, it is told someone else is live and refused outright. It should have resolved A's stale attempt and claimed the ref itself.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "same temp copy: bun test ./leases.test.ts -t \"review regression: run B reconciles\"",
    "output": "B result: {\"kind\":\"refused\",\"reason\":\"live\"}\nExpected: \"held\" Received: \"refused\"\n(fail) review regression: run B reconciles run A's unapplied pending acquisition first"
   },
   "evidence": "Line 107, `if (row && row.runId !== want.run && (row.intent || row.confirmed?.state === \"held\")) return refused;`, runs before `const settled = await reconcile(repo, ref, signal);` (108). A pending intent from another run therefore returns a definitive `refused: live` without being reconciled. That contradicts invariant 8 (reconcile before every operation; while still unresolved, return `wait`) and invariant 9 (a failed acquisition must not block the next run). HEAD's own test 'fresh lineage refuses an old run still confirmed held or pending' asserts this behaviour, so it was a deliberate choice, but the spec is explicit."
  }
 },
